(B) Slip (b): alpha_d = T + d h with d = floor(LT/2pi); AF Prop 4.2 proof asserts alpha_k notin [T,2T) for k notin [0,d)
   T=   1000: LT/2pi=806.8962  alpha_(d-1)=1997.6500  alpha_d=1998.8894  in [T,2T)? True   2T-alpha_d=1.1106 < h=1.2393
   T=   2000: LT/2pi=1834.4280  alpha_(d-1)=3998.4432  alpha_d=3999.5334  in [T,2T)? True   2T-alpha_d=0.4666 < h=1.0903
   T=  10000: LT/2pi=11733.6398  alpha_(d-1)=19998.6025  alpha_d=19999.4547  in [T,2T)? True   2T-alpha_d=0.5453 < h=0.8523
   T=  30000: LT/2pi=40446.4066  alpha_(d-1)=59998.9567  alpha_d=59999.6984  in [T,2T)? True   2T-alpha_d=0.3016 < h=0.7417
   (analytic) d h = h floor(T/h) in (T-h, T], so alpha_d in (2T-h, 2T], with alpha_d < 2T iff LT/2pi is not an integer.
   For Re gamma in [3T/2, alpha_d): |Re gamma - alpha_d| = D_rho - (2T - alpha_d) < D_rho, but >= D_rho - h.
